// gemv already reads near the iPhone's roofline on the big shapes; the VERIFY kernel does not (each extra row +~22% on the head): with one
// row per thread every row re-reads x for every weight word (8 bytes of x per weight byte per x row), and growing its workgroup memory lost
// every time (occupancy; WebKit also zero-fills every workgroup array at the start of every workgroup). v5:
//   - a thread = ND output ROWS (rt, rt + RT, ..., RT = 64 / ND) x one LANE of groups (lane j: groups g0 + j, g0 + j + L, ... ascending):
//     every x value it loads serves its ND rows (x traffic / ND), every weight word it dequantises serves all M x rows;
//   - weights: one 16-byte load per row per 32-weight group; x: vec4s only; no integer division by a runtime value (WebKit makes those
//     helper calls); the 8 weights of a word meet their x as two vec4 dots;
//   - x either STAGED in workgroup memory with each group's sum(x) (made in the same pass; the reduction reuses that memory), or read
//     DIRECT from the storage buffer (no x in workgroup memory; the group sums made in registers); rms in both = x * nw per element and
//     the row's rstd once on its total, so staged and direct make the SAME values (the engine may take either per call);
//   - dequantising: 'shift' (as v4); 'mask' (x pre-scaled by 2^-4i so a mask alone dequantises: the same products, so the same sums as
//     'shift'); 'u8' (unpack4xU8 of the even / odd nibbles, x arranged to match, the odd ones pre-scaled by 1/16);
